(PART E — LT POWER AND CONTROL CABLES) Tj T*
(\(a\) LT power cables shall be XLPE insulated 1.1 kV grade armoured cables with aluminium) Tj T*
(conductors as per IS 7098 \(Part 1\):1988.) Tj T*
(\(b\) Continuous conductor operating temperature of XLPE cables shall be 90 deg C. COPPER CONTROL) Tj T*
(CABLES OF 2.5 SQ MM SHALL BE PVC INSULATED HEAVY DUTY TYPE AS PER IS 1554 \(PART 1\).) Tj T*
(\(c\) Cable conductors shall meet the resistance requirements of IS 8130 for class 2 conductors.) Tj T*
(\(d\) Cables shall be laid directly in ground at a depth of 750 mm. with brick protection.) Tj T*
(\(e\) Terminations shall be made with brass double compression glands and tinned copper lugs.) Tj T*
(\(f\) Cable drums shall carry marking of size, type, length and manufacturer's name.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 6: TESTING, INSPECTION AND CERTIFICATION) Tj T*
(\(a\) EACH SWITCHBOARD SHALL BE SUBJECTED TO ROUTINE VERIFICATION TESTS AS PER IS/IEC 61439-2 AT) Tj T*
(THE WORKS.) Tj T*
(\(b\) The bidder shall furnish type test reports of the switchboard and breakers from an NABL) Tj T*
(accredited laboratory.) Tj T*
(\(c\) Acceptance tests on cables shall be carried out as per IS 10810 in presence of the) Tj T*
(Engineer.) Tj T*
(\(d\) Manufacturer's test certificates shall accompany every cable drum supplied.) Tj T*
(\(e\) Pre-dispatch inspection shall be offered to the Department's authorised representative with) Tj T*
(15 days notice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(\(a\) Shop drawings and schematic diagrams shall be got approved from the Engineer-in-charge) Tj T*
() Tj T*
